Subject: register VM: deferred-RC exact-count fixes and back-edge zero-count drain (stage D3)

What this does:
  Stage D3 of the deferred-RC plan
  (`HP-S3-DEFERRED-RC-PLAN-2026-10-02.md` section 3) does two things.

  (1) Exact-count fixes. Under deferred RC a value can be referenced from a
  register without that register owning it, so a bare `JS_REF_COUNT(x) == 1`
  test no longer proves the value is uniquely owned. Add
  `JS_DRC_UNIQUELY_OWNED(p)` (`ref_count == 1 && !in_zct`) and use it in the
  `JS_ConcatString2` in-place append; guard `js_accum_append` against a parked
  value; and skip the `js_closcyc_frame` closure self-cycle break under
  `QJS_DRC` (leave the cycle to the collector, which can see the
  closure -> var_ref edge). With owning registers these are conservative
  no-ops, but they are what makes the operations correct once D4 flips
  registers to stop owning.

  (2) Back-edge zero-count drain. D2's ZCT is only drained from
  `__js_poll_interrupts`, which the register VM calls before in-line calls and
  never at a loop back edge; a call-free allocation loop therefore parks one
  value per iteration and grows the table to the whole iteration count
  (`str.js` peaked at ~1.2 GB). A backward branch is the only frequent, cheap
  and safe drain point inside a register-VM activation (every live value is in
  a register there). `T_NEXT`/`T_BR_NEXT` now call `REGVM_DRC_BACKEDGE`, which
  tests `off < 0` and the table bound inline and, only when both hold,
  tail-calls `regvm_t_safepoint_slow` to reconcile and re-enter the chain at
  the branch target. The inline test is three loads and a compare and the rare
  reconcile is a tail call, so branch handlers stay frameless.

  Measured (`fixed.js`): stage cost vs the same tree with `-DQJS_DRC=0` is
  about +185-340M instructions (+0.6-1.2%), the D1+D2+D3 infrastructure;
  all of it is removed again by D4. `str.js` peak RSS drops from 1,199,288 KB
  to 175,064 KB and an object-churn loop stays at 4,236 KB. All gates pass:
  checksum `546.1008391043414`, diff-suite `pass=398 fail=0 skip=0` mono and
  threaded, leak check clean, ASan+UBSan clean, no new test262 failures.

